## tools

the light phone calls its features "tools", and these are my thoughts about the tools i have installed so far.

### phone

there is not a lot to complain about. this is the calling and SMS feature. calling works flawlessly. SMS has a few problems though. when responding to a message, you cannot see what the other person sent you to begin with, so you have to keep it in your head. let's say you have a conversation with very long text messages. it is a struggle to answer, because you have to keep the whole context in your head. and then there is no autocorrect. these are the main issues.

### alarm

it is an alarm. and with this phone i only set one alarm each morning, and i actually wake up. i used to set multiple alarms with my smartphone. why is it different? i honestly don't know. maybe i take my dumb phone more seriously?

### album

shows the pictures, and you can easily forward them to your mail account. that is really nice. it makes transferring images very simple from a user experience standpoint.

### calendar

it has the features you want from a calendar. you can set reminders, attach an address for where something takes place, and add notes. but it seems like you cannot edit event notes afterward. that is the only downside, because i wanted to do that the other day.

### camera

i have only used the photo mode, so not video or selfie mode. and i have only taken four photos so far. the only confusing thing is how you take the actual photo. the UX could be better. but it works, and the quality is ok. i will attach the photos i have taken.

